WEBVTT

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:12.140
To fight against messengers from the future who are changing history to erase soccer...

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.510
...we, the Raimon Eleven, are now traveling through time to assemble the strongest eleven in history.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:29.340
No way!

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.160
Wondeba!

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.190
These insolent knaves were plotting to kill you, Nobunaga-sama!

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.220
Look! Here is the proof!

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.900
That's Protocol Omega's...

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.920
We will now begin the interrogation.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.540
Raise your heads.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.930
So you do work for Imagawa after all.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:41.430
Tenma...

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.340
Excuse me! Excuse me!

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:47.470
Takuto-sama!

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.980
Are you here to assassinate me?

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.830
Can you not even fabricate an excuse?

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:56.480
You're wrong!

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.030
Tenma!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.350
We would never assassinate you!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.780
Then why have you entered this banquet without my invitation?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.760
The first time, you named yourselves fireworks craftsmen and approached me.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.170
Now you have stolen in here as dancers.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.290
And you still wish to claim that you do not have an ulterior motive?

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.880
T-That's because...

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.010
Dummy! Think first before you answer!

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.970
Since you cannot answer me, you must be...

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:25.590
Nobunaga-sama!

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.060
We have traveled here through time!

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.150
Traveled through time?

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.510
Yes!

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:40.240
We've come from a world that is far, far into the future.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.630
The future?

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.420
Then...

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.580
When he said he came from a different place...

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.080
Takuto-sama...

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.430
Such nonsense!

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:58.500
You must be laughing at us to think that we would be so deceived!

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.170
My lord, these hooligans do not even deserve to be interrogated!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.760
They should all be put to death!

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.890
Put to death?!

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:08.100
Take them away!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.960
Now, wait, this is interesting.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.890
But, my lord!

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:19.440
Your explanation does not satisfy me.

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:23.650
If you are from the future, describe it in a way that I may understand.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.000
That you may understand?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.160
The future we've come from is...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:36.350
...the country of Japan that is a couple of hundreds of years from now, after it has met with much progress.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:42.840
We have traveled to this era much like how one would ride a boat across the seas.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:45.560
That's impossible!

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.060
Then? What is the state of the future Japan?

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.170
The state?

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:57.180
It is a peaceful and bountiful country with no wars to threaten it.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.570
So Japan gets better?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.110
Yes!

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:07.700
If you truly have come from the future, then you would know what is to occur here, correct?

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.990
Yes, we would know the major events of this era.

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:13.910
Then tell me this.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.610
Do I, Oda Nobunaga...

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.250
...rule the country?

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.880
Well? Answer me.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:32.560
Unfortunately, Nobunaga-sama, you do not.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:34.040
Shindou!

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.580
Impossible...

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.810
Nobunaga-sama does not rule?

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.800
Insolent wretch!

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:42.230
I see.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.280
That is a shame.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:49.740
What's going on?

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.660
What? Are we saved?

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.660
Then it's time to execute our next move.

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:58.710
Let's go.

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.140
Who are you?!

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:08.090
We are Lord Imagawa Yoshimoto's retainers, and we have come to challenge you to a duel.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:09.300
What?

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:10.630
It's them!

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:11.640
Protocol Omega!

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:13.640
We will now read our lord's correspondence.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:16.450
Lord Oda Nobunaga.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:21.860
I have become quite taken by a sport called kemari in which one challenges another through ball-kicking.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:26.860
Thus, why not hold a match through a kemari battle?

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.820
A kemari battle?

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:38.870
It must be an unfeasible concept for Lord Nobunaga to wrap his mind around, when he only has war on the brain, to be sure.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.580
The impudence!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.080
Never mind them, cut them down!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.170
A kemari battle?

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:50.220
Nobunaga-sama!

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.050
Please let us fight for you!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.900
Fighting through kemari is our specialty.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.140
You may rely on me for command!

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.900
You have my word that I will pursue Imagawa's army with efficiency and win!

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.350
Fools! Who would depend on the likes of you!

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:10.200
Very well.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.530
My lord!

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.860
What is your name?

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:14.830
Kinoshita.

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.250
Kinoshita Toukichirou!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.430
The match will be in one week.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:23.490
That is seven days time.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.870
The day of the Fool's Festival!

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:26.750
Fool's Festival?

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:29.520
Nobunaga holds it once a year.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:32.980
It is said to get so rowdy at times that some leave the festival with injuries.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:36.720
They must be planning to crush us using that as a cover.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:43.230
Using people and events that are a part of the era make it harder for a change in the timeline to set off a time paradox.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:46.230
So that's why they're choosing to do it in the middle of the festival.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.230
We look forward to it.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:01.710
It's boiled tofu!

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:05.110
I'm sorry that you had to do all of this for us.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.300
Not at all...

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.590
Eat your fill!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.560
There's plenty of tofu to go around.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.110
Yay!

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.510
It looks delicious!

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.050
Let's eat, let's eat!

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.720
It's delicious!

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.030
Yeah, it's so soft!

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:24.170
Of course it is! My family made this tofu!

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.440
It's a nice color, too.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:31.660
In any case, you sure surprised me when you told him he wouldn't rule the country.

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.910
I didn't think you would tell him the truth.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.340
He doesn't seem like the type to be fooled by superficial lies.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:41.890
Does this mean you're closer to understanding more about Nobunaga?

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:45.080
In that case, your Mixi-max for next time will work for sure!

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.790
No, not yet.

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:51.810
The more I learn about him, the more I grow painfully aware of how different in size our vessels are.

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.340
Shin-sama...

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:56.740
Oh yeah!

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.500
Is it true that you guys came from the future?

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:03.140
Tasuke!

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:05.020
But I want to know!

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.210
Besides, that officer who caught you today was also from the White Deer Gang, isn't she?

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.480
You could tell?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.480
Of course!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:17.100
Do those guys who call themselves Imagawa's retainers have something to do with this, too?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.540
Did I say something wrong?

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:25.580
Maybe it's best that we tell you the truth.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:34.840
Our upcoming battle with Protocol Omega is going to be incomparably more difficult compared to the White Deer Gang.

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:37.110
Then I'll explain.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:41.310
I'll go out to get more tofu.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.950
Tasuke, it's true that we've come from the future.

00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:55.540
The future we're from is hundreds of years ahead.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.490
Hundreds of years?!

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:01.040
In our time, soccer gives dreams to people.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:04.690
But then people showed up trying to take away that soccer from us.

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:07.750
Those guys are the ones who call themselves Imagawa's retainers.

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:12.240
In order to protect soccer, we have to beat them.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.710
But to do that, we need to get stronger.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.190
That's why we've come to this time period.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.590
To borrow Oda Nobunaga's power.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:24.550
Do you think he understood?

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:25.350
No idea...

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.280
Wow!

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.850
So you really have come from the future!

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.020
This is my first time seeing people from the future!

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:35.100
Well, that's normally the case...

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.730
I've made up my mind!

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.370
Let me help you out!

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.430
I know how important soccer is now, too!

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.210
I won't let those guys take it away!

00:10:43.210 --> 00:10:44.580
Tasuke...

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:45.590
Is that okay?

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:46.830
Of course!

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.170
All right, let's do it!

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:52.110
Soccer!

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:05.050
Starting now, we will begin training for the match in one week!

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:08.620
Tasuke! I'm going to come down hard on you, so you'd better be ready!

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:09.560
Please guide me!

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.870
Wondeba-san seems to be in high spirits today, don't you think?

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:17.680
That's because big bro Toukichirou isn't around.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:22.010
He had his position as coach taken out from right under him during the White Deer Gang match, after all.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.140
Oh, so that's why.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.700
Hey!

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.740
Hey!

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.370
Toukichirou-san!

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:29.540
What?!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.720
Soccer is played with eleven people, right?

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:33.670
So I've brought them.

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.480
We didn't play very good in the last match, you see.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:38.450
I'm not going to leave it at that!

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:42.320
Besides, we get to wear those "unifoam" things again, right?

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.680
So, please teach us.

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:45.220
Guys...

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.330
Before we start, I just want to say one thing to you!

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:53.900
I don't believe you when you say Nobunaga-sama doesn't rule the country!

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:56.010
If it isn't Nobunaga-sama, who is it?

00:11:56.010 --> 00:11:57.930
Is it Imagawa? Takeda?

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.150
See, you can't answer me!

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:06.280
You may have Nobunaga-sama fooled, but not me!

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.890
Now, let's begin practice!

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:11.520
Yes, sir!

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:18.170
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.280
Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone!

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.260
Tsurugi!

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:32.800
Tasuke!

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.850
Okay, come on!

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:38.210
Tasuke!

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:40.730
Tasuke, watch the ball more closely!

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:43.220
I'll get it next time!

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.090
Don't run away!

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:50.950
But it's so quick...

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:52.550
I did it!

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:53.660
You're wide open!

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:02.180
About the kemari battle, sir...

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:05.320
Was it such a good idea to leave the matter to that bunch?

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:08.130
They don't appear capable enough to defeat Imagawa.

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:09.130
I don't mind.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.490
But, my lord!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.520
Surely you do not believe their falsehoods about coming from the future!

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:20.040
And if I did?

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.580
I do not rule the country, he says.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.020
Now that is interesting.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.490
Shindou!

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.730
Instrumentalist Maestro!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.350
Okay, use Avatar Armed!

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.030
Armed!

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:47.360
Shindou-senpai!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.090
I'm still missing something!

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:52.900
One more time!

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.140
Armed!

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:04.960
Takuto-sama...

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.450
We're back!

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:09.430
It's hot pot!

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:10.910
Looks terrific!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:14.370
Make sure you eat up and gain energy.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.840
You too, Takuto-sama.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:18.460
O-Okay...

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.170
Sis, the tofu!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.460
Oh right, sorry.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:27.370
It's clear to me how important soccer is to you, Takuto-sama.

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.240
And also, that I cannot keep you here...

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:33.970
So please, let me at least be of use to you while you are here.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.780
Seconds!

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:37.250
Here you go.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.940
Okatsu-san...

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:43.360
Shindou, if you don't hurry up, it'll be all gone!

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.630
R-Right...

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:48.570
There it goes, Ichimasa!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:49.950
Huh?

00:14:58.150 --> 00:14:59.820
Good job, Tasuke!

00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:04.960
I'm not done yet!

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:22.270
Let's go!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:33.480
I got it!

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:35.490
Good job, Ichimasa!

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:41.270
Tasuke!

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.900
They're all improving greatly.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:48.280
Yeah, at this rate, we just might win!

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:54.090
Nice, Shinsuke!

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:56.590
Okay! That's enough practice for today!

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:58.570
It's over!

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.460
Let's go eat!

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.570
I'm starving!

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.200
This isn't good enough.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.040
I have to get better than this!

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.240
Practicing?

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.960
Then I'll help you.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:21.290
Tenma!

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:24.420
Tasuke!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.430
Put more feeling into it when you grab for the ball!

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:28.100
Okay!

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:29.780
Look, to the right!

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:30.710
Now left!

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:33.420
Watch closely at how your opponent moves!

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:42.300
Your movements are getting smaller!

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.310
I'll get it this time!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.890
This is so frustrating...

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:54.520
Why can't I steal the ball from you...

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.570
But your movement has gotten loads better.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.640
It's still not good enough.

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.810
I have to get better than this.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:06.030
The match is the day after tomorrow.

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:09.170
What if I drag everyone else down?

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:11.250
You'll be fine, Tasuke.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:11.820
But...

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:13.900
I'm positive you can do it.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.500
When you kick the ball at me, it feels like the ball is laughing.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.220
The ball, laughing?

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.400
Yeah, like it's having a whole lot of fun.

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:25.180
Tasuke, you like soccer, right?

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:27.320
Yeah, I do!

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:30.540
Then you should trust in soccer.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:34.190
As long as you like soccer, it will answer back to you.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.170
Things will work out somehow.

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:49.200
Somehow, huh?

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:51.460
Yeah, somehow.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:53.420
Yeah...

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.250
Things will work out.

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:58.970
A combo technique?

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:02.030
It's true that Tasuke and the others have vastly improved.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:04.930
Your condition now is a world of difference compared to how you were with the White Deer Gang.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:09.930
But even so, I doubt you will be able to defend against Imagawa's attack completely.

00:18:11.410 --> 00:18:14.820
But coming up with a combo technique now is so sudden...

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.770
The match is tomorrow!

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:18.830
So what!

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:22.460
If war calls for you to make a castle in one night, then you go ahead and do just that!

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:26.160
You won't be able to beat them unless you have that amount of determination!

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:30.500
Besides, tomorrow's match has Nobunaga-sama's honor at stake!

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:31.750
Tasuke.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:33.090
Shishimaru.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:34.380
Gorouta.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:39.560
You three will complete a defense combination technique by tomorrow.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:41.330
It'll be called One-Night Castle!

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:44.820
A castle that is made in one night: One-Night Castle!

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:46.880
One-Night Castle?

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:48.550
That's...

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:51.590
It's the name of a real castle that Hideyoshi made.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:52.830
This one came first...

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.120
One-Night Castle...

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:57.130
I'll do it!

00:18:57.130 --> 00:19:00.700
I'll perfect that One-Night Castle technique, sir!

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:12.170
Let's go, Shishimaru! Gorouta!

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:13.960
One-Night Castle!

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:17.690
Tasuke!

00:19:22.130 --> 00:19:23.620
It's too much for them to handle.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.830
Why can't we do it?

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.780
I won't give up...

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:37.630
I'll take it on.

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.610
Shishimaru and Gorouta, I want you to support me.

00:19:45.770 --> 00:19:47.560
Okay, one more time!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.290
Those guys...

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.160
Again!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:59.800
As long as I like soccer, it will answer back to me.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:00.730
Let's go!

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:02.800
One-Night Castle!

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:10.880
W-We did it...

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:13.940
We did it!

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:16.150
T-That just now...

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:17.650
You did it!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.570
You did it, Tasuke!

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.290
Yeah!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.500
They're all amazing!

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.190
You completed One-Night Castle!

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:28.770
Yes!

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:29.430
We did it!

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.420
A kemari battle?

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:44.670
Should we go see?

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:45.380
Okay.

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:55.050
Well, I see you've actually come.

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:58.190
I commend you for your bravery.

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:02.380
But you've made a poor choice bringing those boys along with you.

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:03.840
We'll make you eat those words!

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.270
You're in for a big surprise if you think we're the same as before!

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:08.880
We'll beat you guys to a pulp!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:10.500
Oh dear...

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:12.280
Don't screw with me!

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:16.530
I'll crush you all with one blow!

00:21:16.530 --> 00:21:18.420
Once this ends, you'll never play soccer again!

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.430
We won't let you!

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.380
We'll protect soccer!

00:22:54.030 --> 00:22:57.850
Soccer, bearing the names of Nobunaga and Imagawa, shatters Sengoku!

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:01.400
Will the Mixi-max work during this fierce fight?

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:04.110
Next, Final Battle at The Fool's Festival!

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:06.320
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:19.250
The Inazuma Eleven GO Chrono Stone's proverb today is...

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:26.570
As long as you like soccer, it will answer back to you!

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:27.550
That's all!
